IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2022 (Western Australia), with what the life events need from the Legal
-- Profession Uniform Law (WA) it applies and from the two sets of Uniform Rules it applies -- how a law graduate gets
-- admitted in WA, gets and keeps a practising certificate, practises under supervision, and who may engage in legal practice.
--
-- SEAT: the law graduate and lawyer (Daniel in the WA cradle-to-grave lives). Every decision is phrased as he would ask it:
-- "Have I met the academic prerequisite?", "May the Supreme Court admit me?", "May I engage in legal practice?", "Must I still
-- practise under supervision?", "Will my late renewal be accepted?". Where a provision addresses only the Legal Practice
-- Board or the Supreme Court, it is encoded as what it means for him. Where the law hands a judgment to the Board or the
-- Court ("if satisfied", "may"), the answer is conditional on that judgment, which is asked as a fact.
--
-- WHICH INSTRUMENT. Every comment and every exported question names its instrument:
--   [Application Act]   Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2022 (WA) -- this subject;
--   [Uniform Law]       Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA), applied by Application Act s 6 (subject wa/legal-profession-uniform-law-wa);
--   [Admission Rules]   Legal Profession Uniform Admission Rules 2015, applied by Application Act s 14(2) as Uniform Rules
--                       (subject wa/legal-profession-uniform-admission-rules-2015);
--   [General Rules]     Legal Profession Uniform General Rules 2015, applied the same way (subject wa/legal-profession-uniform-general-rules-2015).
-- Application Act s 12: if a provision of the Application Act is inconsistent with the Uniform Law, "the provision of this Act
-- prevails".
--
-- Provisions covered: [Application Act] ss 6, 7(1), 12, 14(2), 20, 113, 114, 116(1), 117(1), (3)-(5), 118(3), 276, 278, 279,
-- 289, 322; [Uniform Law] ss 6 ("Australian lawyer", "Australian legal practitioner", "engage in legal practice", "qualified
-- entity", "supervised legal practice" (a)), 10, 12, 16(1), 17(1), 18(1), 19(3), (8), 22(2), 43, 44(1), (3), (4), 45(1), (2),
-- 47(6), 49(1), (3), (4), Sch 4 cll 11, 12 (applied by Application Act s 266(2)(a)); [Admission Rules] rr 5(1), (2), 6(2), (3),
-- (4), Sch 2 cl 4; [General Rules] rr 7(1), 9, 10, 14, 17, 18.
--
-- Edition: [Application Act] compilation from legislation.wa.gov.au (mrdoc 47480), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_47480.txt; no compilation or reprint number shown; its compilation table lists the Act
-- (No. 9 of 2022; Pt 1 in force 14 April 2022, the rest 1 July 2022 under SL 2022/113 cl 2), the Legal Profession Uniform Law
-- Application (Levy) Act 2022 and the Workers Compensation and Injury Management Act 2023 Pt 15 Div 3 Subdiv 8 (1 July 2024).
-- [Uniform Law] legislation.wa.gov.au mrdoc 46913, retrieved 7 September 2026, deposited at
-- ../../../legal-profession-uniform-law-wa/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_46913.txt (the deposit does not show its as-at date).
-- [Admission Rules] mrdoc 49001, version 00-e0-00, currency from 31 October 2025 (compilation table to the Administrative Review
-- Tribunal amendment rule 2025), at ../../../legal-profession-uniform-admission-rules-2015/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_49001.txt.
-- [General Rules] mrdoc 45732, version 00-a0-02, currency from 1 July 2022, at
-- ../../../legal-profession-uniform-general-rules-2015/registers/source-bundle/mrdoc_45732.txt.
-- The local regulations (fees, the standard renewal period, the late fee period) and the Uniform Regulations are not
-- deposited; the periods are INPUTS.
--
-- NOT ENCODED: Part 3 of the Application Act (the Board and committees), registration certificates (ss 120-122), trust
-- accounts, professional indemnity insurance and fidelity cover (Parts 5, 7, 8: whether PII is in place is asked as a fact),
-- proceedings, registers, enforcement and the other transitional provisions; the Uniform Law's foreign-lawyer provisions (ss
-- 20, 58-71), early assessment of suitability (s 21), removal from the roll (s 23), appeals (ss 26-28), conditions other than
-- those named (ss 47(1)-(5), 48, 50-53), show cause events (Part 3.5); the Admission Rules' evidence, disclosure and health
-- provisions (rr 12-25) beyond the matters the Board must weigh (r 10, one fact); Schedules 1 and 2 beyond one fact each; the
-- General Rules' fit-and-proper matters (r 13, one fact), trust money and everything after Part 3.3. The Legal Profession Act
-- 2008 (the "old Act") that governed Daniel's 2020 admission is repealed and not deposited; only the bridges this Act and the
-- Uniform Law's Schedule 4 build from it are encoded. Costs are in lpula-costs.l4.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Written straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill, from the seat of the
-- individual to whom the law is applied, with the design defaults ruled on 2026-10-18. No pipeline, no coverage table, no
-- independent test pass, no human gate. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Legal Profession Uniform Law Application Act 2022 (WA) -- admission and practice`

§§ `dates and helpers`

-- [Application Act] s 7(1): "the Law as in force on 21 June 2021 comes into operation in the State on the day (commencement
-- day) on which this section comes into operation". Compilation table: "Act other than Pt. 1: 1 Jul 2022".
`commencement day` MEANS Date 1 7 2022

GIVEN `a` IS A DATE
      `b` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is on or after` MEANS Day `a` AT LEAST Day `b`

-- The same day of the month `n` months later; a day the later month lacks becomes its last day (31 August + 6 months is
-- 28 or 29 February). Month overflow past December rolls into the next year.
GIVEN `d` IS A DATE
      `n` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`months after` MEANS
    Date (IF DATE_DAY `d` GREATER THAN `last day` THEN `last day` ELSE DATE_DAY `d`)
         (DATE_MONTH `d` PLUS `n`)
         (DATE_YEAR `d`)
    WHERE
        `last day` MEANS Day (Date 1 (DATE_MONTH `d` PLUS `n` PLUS 1) (DATE_YEAR `d`))
                   MINUS Day (Date 1 (DATE_MONTH `d` PLUS `n`) (DATE_YEAR `d`))

-- Whole calendar months from one date to a later one.
GIVEN `from` IS A DATE
      `to`   IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`whole months from` MEANS
    (DATE_YEAR `to` MINUS DATE_YEAR `from`) TIMES 12
    PLUS DATE_MONTH `to` MINUS DATE_MONTH `from`
    MINUS (IF DATE_DAY `to` LESS THAN DATE_DAY `from` THEN 1 ELSE 0)

-- [General Rules] r 17(1): a certificate is in force "until the end of the following 30 June".
GIVEN `d` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the 30 June following` MEANS
    IF DATE_MONTH `d` AT MOST 6 THEN Date 30 6 (DATE_YEAR `d`) ELSE Date 30 6 (DATE_YEAR `d` PLUS 1)

@export Does the Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA) govern my admission and practice on this date (Application Act ss 6, 7)?
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE @desc The date you are asking about
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the Uniform Law govern my admission and practice on` IF
    `is on or after` `the date` `commencement day`

§§ `20 -- who decides`

-- [Application Act] s 20 Table: the designated local regulatory authority for "Part 2.2" (admission) and "Chapter 3, other
-- than section 82(4)" (practising certificates) is the "Board" (the Legal Practice Board); for "Section 82(4)" it is the Legal
-- Services and Complaints Committee. s 21: the Principal Registrar is the designated local roll authority.
-- [Admission Rules] r 4: "Board means the person or body specified ... as the designated local regulatory authority".
DECLARE `What I want decided` IS ONE OF
    `my compliance certificate for admission`
    `my practising certificate`
    `action against my certificate under Uniform Law s 82(4)`

DECLARE `Decision maker` IS ONE OF
    `the Legal Practice Board`
    `the Legal Services and Complaints Committee`

@export Who decides this for me in WA (Application Act s 20)?
GIVEN `the matter` IS A `What I want decided` @desc What you want decided
GIVETH A `Decision maker`
DECIDE `Who decides this for me` IS
    CONSIDER `the matter`
    WHEN `action against my certificate under Uniform Law s 82(4)` THEN `the Legal Services and Complaints Committee`
    OTHERWISE `the Legal Practice Board`

§§ `Admission Rules r 5 -- the academic qualifications prerequisite`

-- [Uniform Law] s 17(1)(a): the prerequisite is "the academic qualifications specified under the Admission Rules".
-- [Admission Rules] r 5(1): "successfully completing a tertiary academic course in Australia, whether or not leading to a degree
-- in law, which: (a) includes the equivalent of at least 3 years' full-time study of law, (b) is accredited by the Board, and
-- (c) the Board determines will provide for a student to acquire and demonstrate appropriate understanding and competence in
-- each element of the academic areas of knowledge set out in Schedule 1". r 7(4) deems another jurisdiction's recognised course
-- accredited; that is folded into "accredited". Schedule 1 lists the eleven areas (criminal law to ethics); one fact here.
-- [Application Act] s 278: approved or corresponding academic qualifications under the old Act obtained "before commencement
-- day" are "taken ... to have attained" the s 17(1)(a) qualifications.
DECLARE `My law course` HAS
    `I completed it successfully`                              IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 5(1)
    `a tertiary academic course in Australia`                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 5(1)
    `years of full-time law study it equals`                   IS A NUMBER   -- r 5(1)(a)
    `accredited by the Board`                                  IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 5(1)(b), r 7(4)
    `the Board determines it covers each Schedule 1 area`      IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 5(1)(c)

@export Have I attained the academic qualifications prerequisite for admission (Uniform Law s 17(1)(a), Admission Rules r 5(1), Application Act s 278)?
GIVEN `the course` IS A `My law course` @desc Your law degree or other law course
      `old Act qualifications obtained before 1 July 2022` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you obtained approved or corresponding academic qualifications under the Legal Profession Act 2008 before 1 July 2022
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I attained the academic qualifications prerequisite` IF
        (    `the course`'s `I completed it successfully`
         AND `the course`'s `a tertiary academic course in Australia`
         AND `the course`'s `years of full-time law study it equals` AT LEAST 3
         AND `the course`'s `accredited by the Board`
         AND `the course`'s `the Board determines it covers each Schedule 1 area`)
    OR  `old Act qualifications obtained before 1 July 2022`

§§ `Admission Rules r 6 -- the practical legal training prerequisite`

-- [Uniform Law] s 17(1)(b): "the practical legal training requirements specified in the Admission Rules".
-- [Admission Rules] r 6(2): "may be satisfied by successfully completing either: (a) a practical legal training course
-- conducted by a practical legal training provider accredited by the Board, or (b) supervised legal training in a workplace for
-- a period of not less than 12 months, under a training plan approved by the Board, which the Board determines adequately
-- provides for the trainee to satisfy the requirements of subrule (1)" (the Schedule 2 competencies).
DECLARE `PLT form` IS ONE OF
    `a PLT course with an accredited provider`   -- r 6(2)(a)
    `supervised legal training in a workplace`   -- r 6(2)(b)
    `no PLT`

DECLARE `My practical legal training` HAS
    `form`                                                     IS A `PLT form`
    `I completed it successfully`                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of supervised legal training under an approved plan` IS A NUMBER -- r 6(2)(b)
    `the Board determines the training plan is adequate`       IS A BOOLEAN  -- r 6(2)(b)

-- [Application Act] s 279(2): old-Act PLT "satisfactorily completed ... before commencement day" counts for s 17(1)(b).
-- s 279(3), (4): PLT "partially completed ... before commencement day" and completed "within the period of 12 months beginning on
-- commencement day" counts "from when the person completes the requirements". The 12 months end on 30 June 2023.
@export Does Application Act s 279 carry my practical legal training under the old Act into the Uniform Law?
GIVEN `I began it before 1 July 2022` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you began old-Act practical legal training before 1 July 2022
      `the date I completed it` IS A DATE @desc The date you completed it
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does section 279 carry my old PLT over` IF
        `I began it before 1 July 2022`
    AND Day `the date I completed it` LESS THAN Day (`months after` `commencement day` 12)

@export Have I completed the practical legal training prerequisite for admission (Uniform Law s 17(1)(b), Admission Rules r 6(2))?
GIVEN `the training` IS A `My practical legal training` @desc Your practical legal training
      `carried over by section 279` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Application Act s 279 carries your old-Act training over
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Have I completed the practical legal training prerequisite` IF
        (    `the training`'s `I completed it successfully`
         AND CONSIDER `the training`'s `form`
             WHEN `a PLT course with an accredited provider` THEN TRUE
             WHEN `supervised legal training in a workplace` THEN
                     `the training`'s `months of supervised legal training under an approved plan` AT LEAST 12
                 AND `the training`'s `the Board determines the training plan is adequate`
             OTHERWISE FALSE)
    OR  `carried over by section 279`

§§ `Admission Rules Sch 2 cl 4 -- when I may start PLT`

-- [Admission Rules] r 6(3): eligible to commence "in the circumstances set out in item 4 of Schedule 2, or when otherwise
-- determined by the Board". Sch 2 cl 4(1): "(a) in the case of SLT, only after the applicant has completed a law course,
-- accredited, or deemed to be accredited ... (b) in the case of a PLT course that is not integrated with the applicant's
-- academic study of law, only after the applicant has completed [such] a law course ... unless the applicant has no more than
-- two academic subjects to complete: (i) neither of which is one of the academic areas of knowledge set out in Schedule 1, and
-- (ii) for which the applicant must be enrolled while undertaking the PLT course, and the applicant has received the prior
-- permission of the Board". cl 4(2): an integrated program of academic study and PLT.
@export May I start my practical legal training now (Admission Rules r 6(3), Schedule 2 cl 4)?
GIVEN `the form` IS A `PLT form` @desc The form of PLT you want to start
      `I have completed an accredited law course` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you have completed your accredited law course
      `academic subjects left` IS A NUMBER @desc How many academic subjects you still have to complete
      `one of them is a Schedule 1 area` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether any subject left is one of the Schedule 1 academic areas
      `enrolled in them during the PLT` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you will be enrolled in them while doing the PLT course
      `the Board gave prior permission` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has given you prior permission
      `an integrated program` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the PLT is part of an integrated program of academic study and PLT
      `the Board otherwise determined` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has otherwise determined you may start
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I start my PLT now` IF
        `the Board otherwise determined`
    OR  CONSIDER `the form`
        WHEN `supervised legal training in a workplace` THEN `I have completed an accredited law course`
        WHEN `a PLT course with an accredited provider` THEN
                `an integrated program`
            OR  `I have completed an accredited law course`
            OR  (    `academic subjects left` AT MOST 2
                 AND (NOT `one of them is a Schedule 1 area`)
                 AND `enrolled in them during the PLT`
                 AND `the Board gave prior permission`)
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Admission Rules rr 5(2), 6(4) -- a qualification more than 5 years old`

-- [Admission Rules] r 5(2): if the academic prerequisite was attained "more than 5 years before applying for a compliance
-- certificate", the Board "may require the applicant to: (a) undertake any further academic subjects, (b) pass any further
-- examinations, and (c) apply for a compliance certificate within any period". r 6(4): the same for PLT completed more than 5
-- years before. Whether the Board does require more is its decision; this asks only whether it may.
@export Can the Board require more study or training of me because I qualified more than 5 years before applying (Admission Rules rr 5(2), 6(4))?
GIVEN `the date I completed it` IS A DATE @desc The date you completed the law course (or the PLT)
      `the date I apply` IS A DATE @desc The date you apply for a compliance certificate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can the Board require more because my qualification is old` IF
    Day `the date I completed it` LESS THAN
        Day (Date (DATE_DAY `the date I apply`) (DATE_MONTH `the date I apply`) (DATE_YEAR `the date I apply` MINUS 5))

§§ `Uniform Law ss 17-19 -- the compliance certificate`

-- [Uniform Law] s 17(1)(c): the person "is a fit and proper person to be admitted"; s 17(2)(b) and [Admission Rules] r 10: the
-- Board "must have regard to" the listed matters (character, disclosure, police report, bankruptcy, offences, English, ...).
-- s 18(1): the Board "may exempt" a person from either prerequisite if satisfied of "sufficient legal skills or relevant
-- experience". s 19(3): the Board "may issue and provide to the Supreme Court a compliance certificate" stating it is satisfied
-- of the prerequisites (or an exemption) and of fitness. s 19(8): it "is not to issue a compliance certificate until after it"
-- has published notice of the application, afforded a reasonable opportunity to object, given the applicant each relevant
-- objection with an opportunity to respond, and considered them.
DECLARE `Compliance certificate answer` IS ONE OF
    `the Board may issue it to the Supreme Court`
    `not yet: the academic qualifications prerequisite is not met and I am not exempt`
    `not yet: the practical legal training prerequisite is not met and I am not exempt`
    `no: the Board is not satisfied I am a fit and proper person`
    `not yet: notice of my application and the objection process are not complete`

@export Can the Board issue me a compliance certificate for admission (Uniform Law ss 17-19, Admission Rules rr 5, 6, 10)?
GIVEN `the course` IS A `My law course` @desc Your law course
      `old Act qualifications obtained before 1 July 2022` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you obtained old-Act academic qualifications before 1 July 2022
      `the training` IS A `My practical legal training` @desc Your practical legal training
      `carried over by section 279` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether Application Act s 279 carries your old-Act training over
      `exempted from the academic prerequisite` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has exempted you under Uniform Law s 18
      `exempted from the PLT prerequisite` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has exempted you under Uniform Law s 18
      `the Board is satisfied I am fit and proper` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board is satisfied you are a fit and proper person
      `notice given and objections dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has published notice and dealt with any objections (s 19(8))
GIVETH A `Compliance certificate answer`
DECIDE `Can the Board issue me a compliance certificate` IS
    IF (NOT `Have I attained the academic qualifications prerequisite` `the course` `old Act qualifications obtained before 1 July 2022`)
       AND (NOT `exempted from the academic prerequisite`)
    THEN `not yet: the academic qualifications prerequisite is not met and I am not exempt`
    ELSE IF (NOT `Have I completed the practical legal training prerequisite` `the training` `carried over by section 279`)
            AND (NOT `exempted from the PLT prerequisite`)
         THEN `not yet: the practical legal training prerequisite is not met and I am not exempt`
         ELSE IF NOT `the Board is satisfied I am fit and proper`
              THEN `no: the Board is not satisfied I am a fit and proper person`
              ELSE IF NOT `notice given and objections dealt with`
                   THEN `not yet: notice of my application and the objection process are not complete`
                   ELSE `the Board may issue it to the Supreme Court`

§§ `Uniform Law s 16, Application Act ss 113, 114, 276 -- admission by the Supreme Court`

-- [Uniform Law] s 16(1): the Supreme Court "may admit an individual aged 18 years or over ... but only if -- (a) the designated
-- local regulatory authority has provided the Supreme Court with a compliance certificate ... and the certificate is still in
-- force; and (b) the person is not already admitted to the Australian legal profession; and (c) the person takes an oath of
-- office, or makes an affirmation of office". s 16(2): residence in the State "is not a requirement". s 16(4): nothing
-- interferes "with the inherent jurisdiction of the Supreme Court to refuse admission" -- so a "may admit" answer is never a
-- promise.
-- [Application Act] s 113: the application is made "(a) in accordance with -- (i) the local regulations; and (ii) the Supreme
-- Court's rules of court; and (iii) a practice direction ... and (b) by paying the fee (if any) prescribed".
-- s 114: "The Supreme Court must be constituted by at least 3 judges when admitting an individual".
DECLARE `My admission application` HAS
    `made in accordance with the local regulations`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in accordance with the rules of court`      IS A BOOLEAN
    `made in accordance with a practice direction`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `a fee is prescribed`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `I paid the prescribed fee`                       IS A BOOLEAN

DECLARE `Admission answer` IS ONE OF
    `the Supreme Court may admit me, subject to its inherent jurisdiction to refuse`
    `no: I am under 18`
    `no: no compliance certificate in force has been provided to the Court`
    `no: I am already admitted`
    `no: I have not taken the oath or made the affirmation of office`
    `no: my application does not meet Application Act s 113`
    `no: the Court is not constituted by at least 3 judges`

GIVEN `born on` IS A DATE
      `on`      IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`age in completed years` MEANS
    IF     DATE_MONTH `on` GREATER THAN DATE_MONTH `born on`
        OR (DATE_MONTH `on` EQUALS DATE_MONTH `born on` AND DATE_DAY `on` AT LEAST DATE_DAY `born on`)
    THEN DATE_YEAR `on` MINUS DATE_YEAR `born on`
    ELSE DATE_YEAR `on` MINUS DATE_YEAR `born on` MINUS 1

@export May the Supreme Court of WA admit me as an Australian lawyer (Uniform Law s 16, Application Act ss 113, 114)?
GIVEN `my date of birth` IS A DATE @desc Your date of birth
      `the admission date` IS A DATE @desc The date of the admission sitting
      `a compliance certificate in force` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has provided the Court with a compliance certificate that is still in force
      `already admitted` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are already admitted to the Australian legal profession
      `I take the oath or affirmation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you take the oath or make the affirmation of office
      `the application` IS A `My admission application` @desc How you applied for admission
      `judges sitting` IS A NUMBER @desc How many judges constitute the Court
GIVETH AN `Admission answer`
DECIDE `May the Supreme Court admit me` IS
    IF `age in completed years` `my date of birth` `the admission date` LESS THAN 18
    THEN `no: I am under 18`
    ELSE IF NOT `a compliance certificate in force`
         THEN `no: no compliance certificate in force has been provided to the Court`
         ELSE IF `already admitted`
              THEN `no: I am already admitted`
              ELSE IF NOT `I take the oath or affirmation`
                   THEN `no: I have not taken the oath or made the affirmation of office`
                   ELSE IF NOT (    `the application`'s `made in accordance with the local regulations`
                                AND `the application`'s `made in accordance with the rules of court`
                                AND `the application`'s `made in accordance with a practice direction`
                                AND ((NOT `the application`'s `a fee is prescribed`) OR `the application`'s `I paid the prescribed fee`))
                        THEN `no: my application does not meet Application Act s 113`
                        ELSE IF `judges sitting` LESS THAN 3
                             THEN `no: the Court is not constituted by at least 3 judges`
                             ELSE `the Supreme Court may admit me, subject to its inherent jurisdiction to refuse`

-- [Application Act] s 276: an application to the full bench "under section 25(1) of the old Act" that "was not decided under the
-- old Act before commencement day" is "taken, on and from commencement day, to be an application under section 113".
@export Does my admission application under the old Act continue as an application under Application Act s 113 (s 276)?
GIVEN `the date I applied` IS A DATE @desc The date you applied under s 25(1) of the Legal Profession Act 2008
      `decided before 1 July 2022` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it was decided before 1 July 2022
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my old admission application continue` IF
        Day `the date I applied` LESS THAN Day `commencement day`
    AND (NOT `decided before 1 July 2022`)

§§ `Uniform Law ss 6, 22(2), Sch 4 cl 11, Application Act s 322 -- am I an Australian lawyer`

-- [Uniform Law] s 6: "Australian lawyer means a person admitted to the Australian legal profession in this jurisdiction or any
-- other jurisdiction". s 22(2): "A person's admission is effective from the time the person signs the Supreme Court roll."
-- [Application Act] s 322: the old Act roll "continues on and from commencement day as the Supreme Court roll". s 266(2)(a)
-- applies the Uniform Law Sch 4 clauses 11 to 18 "without modification".
-- [Uniform Law] Sch 4 cl 11(1): a person who was a local lawyer under the old legislation "immediately before the commencement
-- day by admission to the legal profession by the Supreme Court is, on and from that day, taken to be an Australian lawyer as if
-- he or she had been admitted ... under this Law"; cl 11(2): "the day of admission ... is the day he or she was previously
-- admitted". (The first-pass encoding of this subject took this as an inference from s 322; Sch 4 cl 11 says it outright.)
DECLARE `My standing` IS ONE OF
    `an Australian lawyer under the Uniform Law (WA)`
    `a lawyer under the old Act: the Uniform Law did not yet apply`
    `not admitted`

@export Am I an Australian lawyer on this date (Uniform Law ss 6, 22(2), Sch 4 cl 11, Application Act s 322)?
GIVEN `the date` IS A DATE @desc The date you are asking about
      `I signed the Supreme Court roll under the Uniform Law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were admitted under the Uniform Law and signed the roll
      `admitted in another Australian jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are admitted in another Australian jurisdiction
      `admitted in WA under the old Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were admitted by the Supreme Court of WA under the Legal Profession Act 2008 (or earlier)
      `removed from the roll` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your name has been removed from the roll
GIVETH A `My standing`
DECIDE `Am I an Australian lawyer` IS
    IF `removed from the roll`
    THEN `not admitted`
    ELSE IF `I signed the Supreme Court roll under the Uniform Law` OR `admitted in another Australian jurisdiction`
         THEN `an Australian lawyer under the Uniform Law (WA)`
         ELSE IF `admitted in WA under the old Act`
              THEN IF `Does the Uniform Law govern my admission and practice on` `the date`
                   THEN `an Australian lawyer under the Uniform Law (WA)`
                   ELSE `a lawyer under the old Act: the Uniform Law did not yet apply`
              ELSE `not admitted`

@export What is my day of admission, if I was admitted in WA under the old Act (Uniform Law Sch 4 cl 11(2))?
GIVEN `the day I was admitted under the old Act` IS A DATE @desc The day the Supreme Court admitted you under the old Act
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is my day of admission` IS `the day I was admitted under the old Act`

§§ `Uniform Law ss 44, 45, Sch 4 cl 12, Application Act s 116, General Rules rr 17, 18 -- my practising certificate`

-- [Uniform Law] s 15 Note 1: "Admission does not of itself entitle a person to engage in legal practice".
-- s 44(1): the Board "may, on application, grant or renew an Australian practising certificate in respect of a financial year".
-- s 44(4): the application "cannot be made in this jurisdiction unless the applicant reasonably intends that this jurisdiction
-- will be his or her principal place of practice". s 44(5) and [General Rules] r 18(2): an applicant who "does not reasonably
-- intend to engage in legal practice in Australia" during the certificate "may [apply] in any participating jurisdiction".
@export Can I apply in WA for my practising certificate (Uniform Law s 44(4), (5), General Rules r 18)?
GIVEN `I intend WA to be my principal place of practice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reasonably intend WA to be your principal place of practice during the certificate
      `I intend to practise in Australia` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you reasonably intend to engage in legal practice in Australia during the certificate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I apply in WA for my practising certificate` IF
        `I intend WA to be my principal place of practice`
    OR  (NOT `I intend to practise in Australia`)

-- [Uniform Law] s 45(1): the Board "may grant or renew ... only if it is satisfied that the applicant -- (a) is an Australian
-- lawyer; and (b) if required by this Law to have professional indemnity insurance -- has, or will have ... professional
-- indemnity insurance ...; and (c) has indicated in the application that he or she does not hold (and ... does not have a
-- current application for) another Australian practising certificate" in force concurrently. s 45(2): it "must not grant or
-- renew ... if it considers that the applicant is not a fit and proper person" ([General Rules] r 13 lists matters; one fact).
-- [Application Act] s 116(1): the application must be in the local approved form, with the documents the form requires, the
-- prescribed fee (if any), any Guarantee Fund contribution (Uniform Law s 225) and any framework contribution.
DECLARE `My certificate application` HAS
    `in the local approved form, with its documents, fee and contributions` IS A BOOLEAN  -- Application Act s 116(1)
    `I am an Australian lawyer`                                 IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 45(1)(a)
    `I must have professional indemnity insurance`              IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 45(1)(b)
    `I have or will have it`                                    IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 45(1)(b)
    `I hold or have applied for another concurrent certificate` IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 45(1)(c)
    `the Board considers me not a fit and proper person`        IS A BOOLEAN  -- s 45(2)

DECLARE `Certificate answer` IS ONE OF
    `the Board may grant or renew it`
    `no: the application does not meet Application Act s 116`
    `no: I am not an Australian lawyer`
    `no: I lack the professional indemnity insurance the Law requires`
    `no: I hold or have applied for another concurrent certificate`
    `no: the Board considers me not a fit and proper person`

@export Can the Legal Practice Board grant or renew my practising certificate (Uniform Law s 45, Application Act s 116)?
GIVEN `the application` IS A `My certificate application` @desc Your application and your circumstances
GIVETH A `Certificate answer`
DECIDE `Can the Board grant or renew my practising certificate` IS
    IF NOT `the application`'s `in the local approved form, with its documents, fee and contributions`
    THEN `no: the application does not meet Application Act s 116`
    ELSE IF NOT `the application`'s `I am an Australian lawyer`
         THEN `no: I am not an Australian lawyer`
         ELSE IF `the application`'s `I must have professional indemnity insurance` AND (NOT `the application`'s `I have or will have it`)
              THEN `no: I lack the professional indemnity insurance the Law requires`
              ELSE IF `the application`'s `I hold or have applied for another concurrent certificate`
                   THEN `no: I hold or have applied for another concurrent certificate`
                   ELSE IF `the application`'s `the Board considers me not a fit and proper person`
                        THEN `no: the Board considers me not a fit and proper person`
                        ELSE `the Board may grant or renew it`

-- [Uniform Law] Sch 4 cl 12(1): an old-legislation practising certificate "granted ... before the commencement day and expressed
-- to be operative on or after that day is taken ... to be an Australian practising certificate granted in this jurisdiction".
-- cl 12(2): an old-legislation application "not determined before the commencement day" is determined as an application under
-- the Law, and "a practising certificate already held by the applicant remains in force as if it were an Australian practising
-- certificate ... until a new certificate is granted or the application is refused".
DECLARE `Old certificate answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: it is taken to be an Australian practising certificate (Sch 4 cl 12(1))`
    `yes, until my pending application is decided (Sch 4 cl 12(2))`
    `no: nothing carries it over`

@export Is my practising certificate under the old Act taken to be an Australian practising certificate under the Uniform Law (Uniform Law Sch 4 cl 12)?
GIVEN `granted before 1 July 2022 and operative on or after it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your old-Act certificate was granted before 1 July 2022 and expressed to be operative on or after that day
      `an application of mine was undetermined on 1 July 2022` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an old-Act application for a certificate was undetermined on 1 July 2022, while you held a certificate
GIVETH AN `Old certificate answer`
DECIDE `Is my old certificate carried over` IS
    IF `granted before 1 July 2022 and operative on or after it`
    THEN `yes: it is taken to be an Australian practising certificate (Sch 4 cl 12(1))`
    ELSE IF `an application of mine was undetermined on 1 July 2022`
         THEN `yes, until my pending application is decided (Sch 4 cl 12(2))`
         ELSE `no: nothing carries it over`

-- [General Rules] r 17(1): a certificate is in force "(a) if granted, from the commencement date specified in it until the end
-- of the following 30 June, or (b) if renewed, from the date of its renewal until the end of the following 30 June, unless the
-- certificate is earlier suspended, cancelled or surrendered". r 17(2): if a renewal application "has been properly made ...
-- before its expiry but the authority has not determined the application by the following 1 July, the certificate is taken to
-- continue in force" until renewal, refusal or withdrawal. [Uniform Law] s 44(3): it "ceases to be in force if the holder ceases
-- to be an Australian lawyer".
@export Is my practising certificate in force on this date (General Rules r 17, Uniform Law s 44(3))?
GIVEN `the date it took effect` IS A DATE @desc The commencement date in the certificate, or the date of its renewal
      `the date` IS A DATE @desc The date you are asking about
      `renewal properly applied for before expiry and still undecided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you properly applied to renew before expiry and the Board has not yet decided
      `still an Australian lawyer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are still an Australian lawyer
      `suspended, cancelled or surrendered` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the certificate has been suspended, cancelled or surrendered
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my practising certificate in force on` IF
        `is on or after` `the date` `the date it took effect`
    AND (   Day `the date` AT MOST Day (`the 30 June following` `the date it took effect`)
         OR `renewal properly applied for before expiry and still undecided`)
    AND `still an Australian lawyer`
    AND (NOT `suspended, cancelled or surrendered`)

§§ `Uniform Law ss 10, 43, 6, General Rules r 10 -- may I engage in legal practice`

-- [Uniform Law] s 6: "Australian legal practitioner means an Australian lawyer who holds a current Australian practising
-- certificate"; "engage in legal practice includes practise law or provide legal services, but does not include engage in
-- policy work"; "qualified entity means -- (a) an Australian legal practitioner; or (b) a law practice; or (c) [a registered or
-- limited foreign lawyer]; or (d) an individual engaged in legal practice under the authority of a law of the Commonwealth or of a
-- jurisdiction, other than this Law or the Uniform Rules; or (e) [an entity of a kind specified in the Uniform Rules]".
-- s 10(1): "An entity must not engage in legal practice in this jurisdiction, unless it is a qualified entity. Penalty: 250 penalty
-- units or imprisonment for 2 years, or both." s 10(2): it "is not entitled to recover any amount, and must repay any amount
-- received". s 10(3) and [General Rules] r 10(1): declared exemptions (licensed conveyancers, land agents, government officers
-- drawing instruments or appearing, public trustees, industrial organisations) -- one fact.
-- s 43(1): "An Australian legal practitioner is entitled to engage in legal practice in this jurisdiction"; s 43(2): "subject to
-- ... the conditions of the practitioner's Australian practising certificate" (for a new lawyer, s 49 below).
DECLARE `What I want to do` IS ONE OF
    `give legal advice or other legal services`
    `policy work only`

DECLARE `Practice answer` IS ONE OF
    `yes: as an Australian legal practitioner I am entitled to (Uniform Law s 43), subject to my certificate's conditions`
    `yes: I am a qualified entity under another law (Uniform Law s 6, para (d))`
    `yes: I am exempt under General Rules r 10`
    `yes: policy work is not engaging in legal practice (Uniform Law s 6)`
    `no: it would be an offence under Uniform Law s 10(1), and I could keep no fee for it (s 10(2))`

@export May I engage in legal practice in WA (Uniform Law ss 6, 10, 43, General Rules r 10)?
GIVEN `what I want to do` IS A `What I want to do` @desc What you want to do
      `my standing` IS A `My standing` @desc Whether you are an Australian lawyer
      `I hold a current practising certificate` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you hold a current Australian practising certificate
      `authorised by another law` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a law of the Commonwealth or a State, other than the Uniform Law, authorises you to engage in legal practice
      `exempt under General Rules r 10` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a General Rules r 10 exemption covers what you do (for example a licensed conveyancer)
GIVETH A `Practice answer`
DECIDE `May I engage in legal practice` IS
    IF `what I want to do` EQUALS `policy work only`
    THEN `yes: policy work is not engaging in legal practice (Uniform Law s 6)`
    ELSE IF `my standing` EQUALS `an Australian lawyer under the Uniform Law (WA)` AND `I hold a current practising certificate`
         THEN `yes: as an Australian legal practitioner I am entitled to (Uniform Law s 43), subject to my certificate's conditions`
         ELSE IF `authorised by another law`
              THEN `yes: I am a qualified entity under another law (Uniform Law s 6, para (d))`
              ELSE IF `exempt under General Rules r 10`
                   THEN `yes: I am exempt under General Rules r 10`
                   ELSE `no: it would be an offence under Uniform Law s 10(1), and I could keep no fee for it (s 10(2))`

-- [Uniform Law] s 10(1): "Penalty: 250 penalty units or imprisonment for 2 years, or both." The value of a penalty unit is not
-- in the deposit.
@export What is the most I can be fined for engaging in legal practice when not entitled (Uniform Law s 10(1)), in penalty units?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for unqualified practice` IS 250

@export What is the longest I can be imprisoned for engaging in legal practice when not entitled (Uniform Law s 10(1)), in years?
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the longest I can be imprisoned for unqualified practice` IS 2

§§ `Uniform Law s 12, General Rules r 9 -- what may I call myself`

-- [Uniform Law] s 12(1)(a) lists "lawyer, legal practitioner, barrister, solicitor, attorney, counsel or proctor". s 12(2): a
-- person is entitled to use one if "of a class authorised by the Uniform Rules". s 12(3): using one "gives rise to a rebuttable
-- presumption ... that the person represented that he or she is entitled to engage in legal practice".
-- [General Rules] r 9 Table: item 1 "Legal practitioner -- Australian legal practitioner -- All circumstances"; item 2 "...
-- solicitor ..." when the certificate is not "as or in the manner of a barrister only"; item 3 "Barrister" when the certificate
-- was "granted in a fused jurisdiction, or ... in a non-fused jurisdiction" and is barrister-only; item 4 "Counsel -- Australian
-- legal practitioner -- All circumstances". The table has no item for "lawyer": no class is authorised by s 12(2) to use it. For
-- an Australian legal practitioner that costs nothing (he is entitled to practise, so the s 12(3) presumption is true). The
-- General Rules do not define "fused jurisdiction"; whether WA is one is asked as a fact.
DECLARE Title IS ONE OF `legal practitioner`, `solicitor`, `barrister`, `counsel`, `lawyer`

@export Does Uniform Law s 12 and General Rules r 9 entitle me to use this title?
GIVEN `the title` IS A Title @desc The title you want to use
      `I am an Australian legal practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian lawyer with a current practising certificate
      `my certificate is barrister only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your certificate authorises practice as or in the manner of a barrister only
      `granted in a fused jurisdiction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your certificate was granted in a fused jurisdiction
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I entitled to use the title` IF
    `I am an Australian legal practitioner` AND
    CONSIDER `the title`
    WHEN `legal practitioner` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `counsel` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `solicitor` THEN NOT `my certificate is barrister only`
    WHEN `barrister` THEN `granted in a fused jurisdiction` OR `my certificate is barrister only`
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `Uniform Law s 49, General Rules rr 7, 14, Application Act s 289 -- supervised legal practice`

-- [Uniform Law] s 49(1): "the holder must, in this jurisdiction, engage in supervised legal practice only, until the holder has
-- completed -- (a) if the holder completed practical legal training principally under the supervision of an Australian lawyer
-- ... -- a period or periods equivalent to 18 months of supervised legal practice; or (b) if the holder completed other practical
-- legal training ... -- a period or periods equivalent to 2 years". s 49(3): not for a barrister-only certificate. s 49(4): the
-- Board "may (a) exempt ... or (b) reduce a period" if satisfied supervision is not needed or needed for less.
-- [Application Act] s 289(2): the whole period is taken to be completed if, before commencement day, the person "(a) had the
-- required experience (as defined in section 50(1) of the old Act); or (b) was entitled to practise on their own account under
-- the Legal Practitioners Act 1893 or the Legal Practice Act 2003".
DECLARE `How I did my PLT` IS ONE OF
    `principally under the supervision of an Australian lawyer`
    `other practical legal training, such as a PLT course`

@export How many months of supervised legal practice must I complete before I may practise unsupervised (Uniform Law s 49, Application Act s 289(2))?
GIVEN `how` IS A `How I did my PLT` @desc How you completed the practical legal training that qualified you for admission
      `my certificate is barrister only` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your certificate authorises practice as a barrister only
      `the Board exempted me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has exempted you under s 49(4)(a)
      `the Board reduced the period` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has reduced your period under s 49(4)(b)
      `the reduced period in months` IS A NUMBER @desc The reduced period, in months, if the Board reduced it
      `old Act experience before 1 July 2022` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether before 1 July 2022 you had the old Act's required experience or were entitled to practise on your own account
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `How many months of supervised legal practice must I complete` IS
    IF `my certificate is barrister only` OR `the Board exempted me` OR `old Act experience before 1 July 2022`
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF `the Board reduced the period`
         THEN `the reduced period in months`
         ELSE CONSIDER `how`
              WHEN `principally under the supervision of an Australian lawyer` THEN 18
              WHEN `other practical legal training, such as a PLT course` THEN 24

-- [General Rules] r 14(2): the period may be one full-time period, one part-time period "equivalent to the required period worked
-- out on a full-time basis", or two or more periods together; r 14(3): public holidays and "normal periods of leave" count.
-- [Application Act] s 289(1): supervised legal practice under the old Act before commencement day counts as "the same period of
-- supervised legal practice" for s 49(1). So the full-time-equivalent months below include any before 1 July 2022.
@export Must I still engage in supervised legal practice only (Uniform Law s 49(1), General Rules r 14, Application Act s 289(1))?
GIVEN `months required` IS A NUMBER @desc The months of supervised legal practice you must complete
      `full-time-equivalent months completed` IS A NUMBER @desc Full-time-equivalent months of supervised legal practice completed, including any before 1 July 2022 under the old Act
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I still engage in supervised legal practice only` IF
    `full-time-equivalent months completed` LESS THAN `months required`

-- [Uniform Law] s 6, "supervised legal practice" (a): legal practice by an Australian legal practitioner "as an employee of ...
-- a law practice, where -- (i) at least one legal practitioner associate of the law practice is an authorised principal; and (ii)
-- the person engages in legal practice under the supervision of an authorised principal". [General Rules] r 7(1): for an
-- employee it "includes supervision by an employee of the law practice who holds an Australian practising certificate
-- authorising the holder to supervise legal practice by others". Paragraphs (b)-(d) and r 7(2) are not encoded.
@export Is my work as an employee of a law practice supervised legal practice (Uniform Law s 6, General Rules r 7(1))?
GIVEN `I am an Australian legal practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are an Australian lawyer with a current practising certificate
      `supervised by an authorised principal` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an authorised principal of the practice supervises you
      `supervised by an employee whose certificate allows supervising` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an employee whose certificate authorises supervising others supervises you
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my work supervised legal practice` IF
        `I am an Australian legal practitioner`
    AND (`supervised by an authorised principal` OR `supervised by an employee whose certificate allows supervising`)

-- [Uniform Law] s 47(6): a certificate "also authorises the holder to supervise legal practice by others. This does not apply --
-- (a) if the certificate is subject to a statutory or discretionary condition that the holder must engage in supervised legal
-- practice only; or (b) to the extent that the certificate is subject to a discretionary condition to the effect that the holder
-- may not supervise".
@export May I supervise other lawyers (Uniform Law s 47(6))?
GIVEN `I must still practise under supervision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether your certificate still requires supervised legal practice only
      `a condition says I may not supervise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether a discretionary condition says you may not supervise
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May I supervise other lawyers` IF
        (NOT `I must still practise under supervision`)
    AND (NOT `a condition says I may not supervise`)

§§ `Application Act ss 117, 118 -- renewing my certificate`

-- [Application Act] s 117(1): a renewal application "must be made within -- (a) the period prescribed by the local regulations as
-- the standard renewal period; or (b) the later period prescribed by the local regulations as the late fee period". s 117(3): the
-- Board "(a) may reject an application for renewal made during the late fee period; and (b) must reject an application for
-- renewal that is not made during the standard renewal period or the late fee period unless the application is accepted under
-- subsection (4)". s 117(4): it "may accept an application made within 6 months after the end of the late fee period (even after
-- the expiry ...)" if satisfied "(a) the delay was caused by matters beyond the control of the applicant; or (b) there are other
-- circumstances warranting acceptance". s 117(7): a late fee may be required. The periods are set by local regulations (not
-- deposited) and are INPUTS; the late fee period is taken to follow the standard period (INFERENCE from "the later period").
DECLARE `Renewal answer` IS ONE OF
    `in time: made in the standard renewal period`
    `late: made in the late fee period, so the Board may reject it and may require a late fee`
    `very late: the Board may accept it only if satisfied the delay was beyond my control or other circumstances warrant it`
    `the Board must reject it`

@export Will the Legal Practice Board accept my renewal application (Application Act s 117)?
GIVEN `the date I lodge it` IS A DATE @desc The date you lodge the renewal application
      `the standard renewal period opens` IS A DATE @desc First day of the standard renewal period (local regulations)
      `the standard renewal period closes` IS A DATE @desc Last day of the standard renewal period (local regulations)
      `the late fee period closes` IS A DATE @desc Last day of the late fee period (local regulations)
GIVETH A `Renewal answer`
DECIDE `Will the Board accept my renewal` IS
    IF Day `the date I lodge it` LESS THAN Day `the standard renewal period opens`
    THEN `the Board must reject it`
    ELSE IF Day `the date I lodge it` AT MOST Day `the standard renewal period closes`
         THEN `in time: made in the standard renewal period`
         ELSE IF Day `the date I lodge it` AT MOST Day `the late fee period closes`
              THEN `late: made in the late fee period, so the Board may reject it and may require a late fee`
              ELSE IF Day `the date I lodge it` AT MOST Day (`months after` `the late fee period closes` 6)
                   THEN `very late: the Board may accept it only if satisfied the delay was beyond my control or other circumstances warrant it`
                   ELSE `the Board must reject it`

-- [Application Act] s 117(5): if accepted under s 117(4) after expiry, the certificate "(a) is taken to have continued in force on
-- and from the 1 July immediately following its expiry ... and (b) if renewed, is taken to have been renewed on and from that
-- 1 July".
@export From what date is my late-renewed certificate taken to have continued in force (Application Act s 117(5))?
GIVEN `the date it expired` IS A DATE @desc The date your certificate expired
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `From when is my late-renewed certificate in force` IS
    IF DATE_MONTH `the date it expired` AT MOST 6
    THEN Date 1 7 (DATE_YEAR `the date it expired`)
    ELSE Date 1 7 (DATE_YEAR `the date it expired` PLUS 1)

-- [Application Act] s 118(3): the Board "is taken to have refused to grant or renew ... if the certificate has not been granted,
-- renewed or refused within 6 months after -- (a) if the Board has given the applicant a notice under the Legal Profession Uniform
-- Law (WA) section 95 -- the day specified in the notice by which the applicant was required to comply ...; or (b) ... the day on
-- which the application ... was lodged". A deemed refusal is what lets the applicant seek review.
@export Am I taken to have been refused my practising certificate (Application Act s 118(3))?
GIVEN `the date I lodged it` IS A DATE @desc The date you lodged the application
      `a section 95 notice was given` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board gave you a notice under Uniform Law s 95
      `the compliance day in the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice required you to comply by (any date if no notice)
      `decided` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the Board has granted, renewed or refused it
      `today` IS A DATE @desc Today's date
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I taken to have been refused` IF
        (NOT `decided`)
    AND Day `today` GREATER THAN Day (`months after` `the start` 6)
    WHERE
        `the start` MEANS IF `a section 95 notice was given` THEN `the compliance day in the notice` ELSE `the date I lodged it`
